WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.010
Speaker 1: I want to start today with something
that's kind of really good news.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:13.400
Some in the audience have grown increasingly
frustrated with me that I have not really

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:24.340
put out my sense of a way to radically deprogram
right wing extremists and reactionaries from

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.029
fact free Trumpism or ignorant political ideas.

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:31.760
Call it what you will, but the question that
we've been kind of grappling with is, OK,

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:32.760
great.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.050
Tens of millions of people think Trump actually
won.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.390
They would vote for him again.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:41.530
They believe untrue things about vaccines
and climate change and the pandemic and all

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.730
these different things.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:43.730
We've identified a problem.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.610
How do we fix it?

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.920
And at the individual level, we know, well,
you know, if you spend three hours, six hours

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.270
with individuals, you can change some minds.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.530
But that's a really difficult thing to do
at a at a sort of large scale.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:02.090
At the same time, when we think about something
from above that radically and quickly changes

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:08.029
views, we're often talking about significant
authoritarianism, which as a progressive,

00:01:08.029 --> 00:01:09.789
I am against authoritarianism.

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:11.280
So we don't really have an answer.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:19.399
But we now have a new study that is really
inspiring and reassuring that it is possible,

00:01:19.399 --> 00:01:22.469
although what we can actually do as a result
remains a question mark.

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:31.759
So I'm talking about a incredible new study
called The Manifold Effects of Partizan Media

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:37.990
on viewers beliefs and attitudes, a field
experiment with Fox News viewers.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.560
And there's a good write up of what this did,
and essentially what they did is they took

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.060
Fox News viewers and they paid them.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.200
They paid them to watch CNN for 30 days.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:57.809
And what they found was that after watching
CNN for 30 days, the Fox News viewers became

00:01:57.809 --> 00:02:05.679
more skeptical about fake actual fake news,
less likely to buy into fake news.

00:02:05.679 --> 00:02:14.319
And they also found changes in attitudes and
policy preferences on COVID 19, on evaluations

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:19.320
of then-President Trump and of Republican
candidates.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.640
And they wrote, and this is so not incredible.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.340
But but it's a good thing.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:30.209
Despite regular Fox News viewers being largely
strong partizans, we found manifold effects

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:38.040
of changing the slant of their media diets
on their factual beliefs, attitudes, perceptions

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.770
of issues, importance and overall political
views.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:49.489
They write it found that Fox News gave viewers
information about why the disease is not a

00:02:49.489 --> 00:02:54.840
serious threat, while CNN provided more information
about the disease itself.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:00.650
This changed people's views and it goes on,
and it says a lot more about what was done

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:01.650
here.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:06.109
And this is important for so many different
reasons now, obviously.

00:03:06.109 --> 00:03:11.700
If you think CNN is bad and not trustworthy
on the facts, then you would see this as bad.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:17.010
You would say, Wow, they they believe the
right things when they watch Fox News.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.749
And after 30 days of watching CNN, all of
a sudden they believe all these liberal lies

00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:22.739
now on these particular issues.

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:27.730
We know during the pandemic, when Trump was
president, Fox News was giving a very skewed

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:31.019
perspective of the pandemic and about other
issues.

00:03:31.019 --> 00:03:36.200
So you can argue as to whether it's a good
thing or not that they end up believing what

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.920
they see on CNN rather than what they see
on Fox.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.450
But that's not the issue I want to focus in
on.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:47.849
The incredible good news is if we put the
right information in front of people, we can

00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:49.920
debate what the right information is.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.760
But if we put the right information, if we
put accurate information in front of people,

00:03:54.760 --> 00:04:00.930
their beliefs are not as resistant to revision
as we might have thought.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:06.330
And the other kind of scary aspect of this
is it reminds us of the significant impact

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.510
of one's media diet.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.510
It's incredible.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.510
Or maybe not.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:15.569
Maybe we say it's disturbing what happens
to people's beliefs when their media diet

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:22.030
is restricted to what we might call extremist
media or disinformation media?

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:32.240
And to some extent, I will gladly concede
that CNN profits off of and depends on fear

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.750
mongering salacious stories.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:40.310
The kind of if it bleeds, it leads the most
extremist and hyperbolic interpretation of

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:45.670
things with a different perspective than Fox
News, but CNN is nowhere near as dishonest.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:51.610
We have to understand the kind of corporate
fear leads framing when I was on my flight

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:52.610
to Las Vegas.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:57.690
In fact, there was a guy sitting across the
aisle from me and I was a long flight from

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:58.710
the East Coast.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:06.030
Five and a half six hours, I watched him consume
hours of Fox News, but then later in the flight,

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:13.280
I looked over and MSNBC was on, and it was
interesting because I was reading this study

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.500
on the flight as I was watching the sky.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:22.970
And we might wrongly say, Well, the MSNBC's
is going to have no impact on the guy.

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:24.940
And what the study shows is that it does.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:31.290
Now again, MSNBC is a not as dishonest.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:37.500
Editorially liberal corporate media outlets,
so for me, MSNBC is not exactly the solution

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:45.069
to Fox News and what this gets me back to,
as many people are kind of addicted to outrage,

00:05:45.069 --> 00:05:52.280
fear, anger and validation of their existing
views as well, because the anger gives people

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.310
sometimes what is like a temporary relief
from what are maybe more difficult feelings

00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:01.820
to deal with, you know, despair in their lives
or a feeling of helplessness, helplessness

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.599
or whatever the case may be.

00:06:03.599 --> 00:06:08.389
Conspiracy content, as we've talked about
before, is sometimes soothing to people because

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:12.860
they would rather believe everything is planned
and orchestrated rather than there are random

